      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nClarify the `CacheConfig.compute_hash()` docstring to reflect the current opt-out hashing implementation.\n\nRelated to #39479 (TODO #7). This complements #46714, which addresses misleading docstrings in other configuration classes.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Remove outdated guidance instructing developers to manually include new fields in the hash factors list.\n- Clarify that dataclass fields are included by default unless explicitly excluded through `ignored_factors`.\n- Document that new fields should only be excluded when doing so is safe for compilation-cache correctness.\n- Preserve existing hashing behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Reviewed the diff to confirm that only the docstring in `vllm/config/cache.py` changed.\n- No runtime tests executed because this is a documentation-only change.\n\n## Details\n\n`CacheConfig.compute_hash()` uses `get_hash_factors(self, ignored_factors)`, which automatically includes dataclass fields unless explicitly excluded.\n\nThe previous docstring described an older opt-in approach where developers had to manually add hash-relevant fields. This update aligns the documentation with the current implementation.\n\nUnlike #46714, this change specifically addresses `CacheConfig`, which computes a hash from its non-excluded configuration fields.\n\n**AI Assistance:** ChatGPT was used to understand the hashing implementation and draft the docstring correction. The final change was manually reviewed.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
